---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="For school and college ceramics departments"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and semester courses for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
				<h1>A ceramics room that runs on the timetable.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Kilnbook takes a school ceramics department from the first wheel booking to the last kiln
					pickup. Students reserve wheels between classes, every piece is tracked through the kiln,
					and each semester's courses have their own roster.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
			<h2>Built for one or two kilns and a full semester</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheels between classes</h3>
					<p>
						Students reserve wheels and hand-building tables in one-hour blocks, so a free period
						means time on a wheel instead of a queue at the door. You set how many hours each group
						gets and how far ahead they can book.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Firings you can follow</h3>
					<p>
						Students log a piece from their phone when it goes on the bisque shelf. Each kiln has its
						own queue and firing log, and students get a text when their work is ready to collect.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Courses for the semester</h3>
					<p>
						Set up each course as a fixed series that runs for the term. Instructors see today's
						roster, mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next teacher.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Which plan fits a school?</h2>
		<p>
			Most departments with one or two kilns fit the Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, and pickup texts when pieces come out of the
			kiln. A room with a single kiln can start on Starter. School ceramics programs get 30% off any
			plan. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>How many kilns does the Studio plan cover?</summary>
				<p>
					Up to 3 kilns, so a department with one or two kilns has room to add another. If you ever
					need more, the Collective plan has no kiln limit.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Is there a discount for schools?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can students book wheels from their phones?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Students reserve wheels and tables in one-hour blocks and log their pieces for firing
					from a phone. Put a tablet by the door and they can check in when they arrive, so you
					always know who is in the room while the kilns are running.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your ceramics room off the whiteboard.</h2>
			<p>See your kilns, wheels and semester courses in Kilnbook on a 20-minute call.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
